1
00:00:00,205 --> 00:00:05,874
FILING FOR LOVE

2
00:00:13,209 --> 00:00:15,002
How could you miss something
this mundane?

3
00:00:15,255 --> 00:00:17,215
Not even a rookie would do this.
Get a hold of yourself!

4
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:19,924
<i>Order within an organization
is built on rank.</i>

5
00:00:25,763 --> 00:00:26,806
<i>However...</i>

6
00:00:28,849 --> 00:00:30,643
<i>the true power game between these two</i>

7
00:00:31,477 --> 00:00:32,979
<i>goes much deeper</i>

8
00:00:33,604 --> 00:00:34,647
<i>and far more quietly.</i>

9
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:46,242
TECHNICAL HIGH SCHOOL

10
00:00:52,498 --> 00:00:54,125
<i>Does a completely equal relationship</i>

11
00:00:54,709 --> 00:00:55,793
<i>even exist?</i>

12
00:01:05,303 --> 00:01:08,264
<i>When two or more come together,
a hierarchy forms.</i>

13
00:01:11,559 --> 00:01:14,145
<i>Even between friends and lovers</i>

14
00:01:14,770 --> 00:01:16,606
<i>an imbalance of power is
almost inevitable.</i>

15
00:01:29,452 --> 00:01:30,536
<i>And everyone</i>

16
00:01:31,329 --> 00:01:33,789
<i>desires to rise higher,
even if only a little.</i>

17
00:01:35,458 --> 00:01:36,459
Good job, everyone.

18
00:01:36,542 --> 00:01:37,585
<i>Sometimes</i>

19
00:01:38,252 --> 00:01:39,962
<i>at the risk of doing things
they shouldn't.</i>

20
00:01:41,964 --> 00:01:43,716
Gosh, that tastes so sweet.

21
00:01:47,887 --> 00:01:48,929
What's that?

22
00:01:49,347 --> 00:01:50,389
- What's what?
- What is it?

23
00:01:52,141 --> 00:01:53,851
- Something's hovering outside.
- Where?

24
00:01:53,934 --> 00:01:54,935
You see something?

25
00:02:02,777 --> 00:02:04,236
You're quite photogenic

26
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,321
Director Kang.

27
00:02:15,122 --> 00:02:16,165
Are you the police?

28
00:02:16,874 --> 00:02:17,875
No, I'm not.

29
00:02:20,086 --> 00:02:21,170
I'm...

30
00:02:56,455 --> 00:02:57,498
NOH KI-JUN

31
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:01,460
I'm with the Audit Team
at the head office.

32
00:03:01,919 --> 00:03:04,046
Stop what you were doing
and follow me for a chat

33
00:03:05,089 --> 00:03:06,215
Director Kang.

34
00:03:09,468 --> 00:03:11,584
INTERVIEW ROOM
AUDIT IN PROGRESS

35
00:03:21,772 --> 00:03:25,651
I heard Haemu's Audit Team
can bring down birds in flight.

36
00:03:27,570 --> 00:03:29,113
I see you send your own birds now.

37
00:03:29,196 --> 00:03:30,865
And you're about to crash and burn.

38
00:03:31,115 --> 00:03:32,491
- Hey, you!
- It's Assistant Manager Noh

39
00:03:32,575 --> 00:03:33,576
from Audit Team One.

40
00:03:33,659 --> 00:03:35,745
How dare an assistant manager
harass a director?

41
00:03:36,328 --> 00:03:37,455
Do you think you're the police?

42
00:03:38,038 --> 00:03:39,165
The National Intelligence Service?

43
00:03:39,457 --> 00:03:41,333
This is illegal filming.

44
00:03:41,959 --> 00:03:45,671
I'll sue you and your whole team
for invasion of privacy.

45
00:03:49,091 --> 00:03:52,386
It's the least I can do to catch
a spy who's selling core tech

46
00:03:53,429 --> 00:03:54,472
to an overseas competitor.

47
00:03:55,681 --> 00:03:57,349
We have our own struggles, too.

48
00:03:57,641 --> 00:03:59,518
It's always the unethical ones
who are obsessed

49
00:04:00,644 --> 00:04:03,397
with privacy and personal rights.

50
00:04:06,358 --> 00:04:07,401
Hey, listen.

51
00:04:08,611 --> 00:04:09,945
Don't go too far.

52
00:04:10,738 --> 00:04:14,158
Even if I were an industrial spy,
this is just my first offense.

53
00:04:14,241 --> 00:04:16,160
So if I act remorseful

54
00:04:16,243 --> 00:04:18,454
I'll most likely be let off
on probation.

55
00:04:24,418 --> 00:04:25,503
Director Kang.

56
00:04:25,586 --> 00:04:27,171
He speaks pretty good Korean,
didn't he?

57
00:04:27,254 --> 00:04:28,714
Because he's an ethnic Korean
from China.

58
00:04:28,798 --> 00:04:30,216
You could say he's Korean.

59
00:04:31,342 --> 00:04:33,844
A North Korean.

60
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:42,228
Turns out this company was
a source of funding for North Korea.

61
00:04:42,812 --> 00:04:44,647
It was disguised
as a foreign-currency operation

62
00:04:45,731 --> 00:04:47,525
but it was actually run
by North Korea.

63
00:04:50,110 --> 00:04:51,111
Oh, dear.

64
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:55,616
If you're charged with espionage,
that means

65
00:04:57,535 --> 00:05:00,287
you're not an industrial spy anymore
but an actual spy.

66
00:05:01,413 --> 00:05:02,456
Probation?

67
00:05:04,583 --> 00:05:06,669
You'll most likely go to prison.

68
00:05:08,295 --> 00:05:09,380
Darn it.

69
00:05:17,721 --> 00:05:19,431
- Oh, no.
- Don't do that.

70
00:05:20,015 --> 00:05:21,350
Will you calm down?

71
00:05:21,433 --> 00:05:22,977
This is so infuriating!

72
00:05:23,352 --> 00:05:26,480
You punks. I said it wasn't me.
Why won't you believe me?

73
00:05:26,564 --> 00:05:28,941
- Calm down, sir. We got a tip-off...
- "Calm down"?

74
00:05:29,191 --> 00:05:31,652
- We got a tip-off.
- A tip-off? What tip-off?

75
00:05:31,777 --> 00:05:33,737
I'm being framed, okay?

76
00:05:34,196 --> 00:05:36,282
Something's always going on
at Team Three.

77
00:05:36,949 --> 00:05:38,242
What is it this time?

78
00:05:38,784 --> 00:05:41,287
Someone sent an anonymous note
to Team Three saying

79
00:05:41,370 --> 00:05:43,414
he hid the fact that he was married
and approached her.

80
00:05:43,497 --> 00:05:46,166
As proof, she said
he has a mole down there.

81
00:05:46,458 --> 00:05:47,793
- What?
- Down there.

82
00:05:47,877 --> 00:05:48,878
Right there.

83
00:05:52,715 --> 00:05:53,757
<i>Haemu Group.</i>

84
00:05:54,633 --> 00:05:56,844
<i>The 7th largest business in Korea
and 9th in sales.</i>

85
00:05:57,428 --> 00:05:59,221
<i>The top-ranking department</i>

86
00:05:59,305 --> 00:06:01,056
<i>in this conglomerate
with 42 subsidiaries.</i>

87
00:06:01,891 --> 00:06:03,267
<i>Even the head office's Audit Team</i>

88
00:06:03,684 --> 00:06:05,644
<i>has a hierarchy of its own.</i>

89
00:06:07,021 --> 00:06:08,814
<i>Audit Team One and Two</i>

90
00:06:08,898 --> 00:06:11,191
<i>handle major cases
such as embezzlement</i>

91
00:06:11,609 --> 00:06:15,070
<i>malpractice, collusion,
and information leaks.</i>

92
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:17,823
<i>Audit Team Three...</i>

93
00:06:17,907 --> 00:06:20,034
I'm not in the mood for coffee!

94
00:06:20,159 --> 00:06:21,785
Okay, fine. Get your hands off me.

95
00:06:21,869 --> 00:06:23,037
- Hands off.
- Okay.

96
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,413
I'll show you.

97
00:06:24,496 --> 00:06:25,956
- No, don't!
- No, don't!

98
00:06:28,042 --> 00:06:29,043
No!

99
00:06:29,126 --> 00:06:30,127
Don't!

100
00:06:30,544 --> 00:06:31,629
Shoot.

101
00:06:31,712 --> 00:06:33,839
- Look!
- Oh, come on...

102
00:06:34,256 --> 00:06:35,299
Look carefully.

103
00:06:35,799 --> 00:06:37,343
Do you see a mole?

104
00:06:37,426 --> 00:06:38,761
- Don't cover it.
- What's his issue?

105
00:06:39,219 --> 00:06:40,262
I'm innocent.

106
00:06:40,554 --> 00:06:42,848
<i>This is what they do.</i>

107
00:06:48,562 --> 00:06:52,483
EPISODE 1:
UP&DOWN

108
00:07:25,182 --> 00:07:26,850
Hello, sir. Good morning.

109
00:07:27,017 --> 00:07:29,770
If it isn't Noh Ki-jun,
the gentleman.

110
00:07:30,312 --> 00:07:32,856
You're having
a handsome start to the day.

111
00:07:33,148 --> 00:07:34,233
Thank you.

112
00:07:34,316 --> 00:07:35,901
- Have a great day.
- You, too.

113
00:07:54,545 --> 00:07:56,005
SAFEGUARDING CORE TECHNOLOGY

114
00:07:56,088 --> 00:07:57,172
FROM INDUSTRIAL SPIES

115
00:07:57,256 --> 00:07:58,757
HAEMU'S AUDIT TEAM

116
00:07:59,341 --> 00:08:02,136
Auditing increases
and improves the value

117
00:08:02,219 --> 00:08:03,929
of the company's business execution.

118
00:08:06,056 --> 00:08:08,350
NOH KI-JUN AKA MR. SMILES,
ASSISTANT MANAGER, AUDIT TEAM 1

119
00:08:09,393 --> 00:08:10,644
Oh, wow.

120
00:08:12,771 --> 00:08:13,772
"Mr. Smiles"?

121
00:08:13,856 --> 00:08:15,232
We can't have those
in the Audit Team.

122
00:08:15,315 --> 00:08:17,317
I didn't come up with it, okay?

123
00:08:17,735 --> 00:08:19,570
What's wrong with it?
It gives me pride

124
00:08:19,653 --> 00:08:22,072
that my colleague is
the face of the Audit Team.

125
00:08:23,032 --> 00:08:25,951
To be honest, Team Three yesterday
was a huge embarrassment.

126
00:08:26,035 --> 00:08:27,870
They let a guy
drop his pants in the office.

127
00:08:27,953 --> 00:08:30,039
It was utter madness.

128
00:08:30,122 --> 00:08:31,290
I dreamed of it, even.

129
00:08:31,373 --> 00:08:33,208
That guy's thing.

130
00:08:33,876 --> 00:08:35,669
- Oh, the shudders.
- Get out of my head.

131
00:08:39,423 --> 00:08:41,675
- It's just <i>gimbap.</i>
- Sorry. My bad.

132
00:08:41,759 --> 00:08:43,218
- Sorry.
- Anyway...

133
00:08:43,302 --> 00:08:46,305
Why should we handle stuff like that?
It's not at all dignified.

134
00:08:46,388 --> 00:08:48,098
We must look into everything
we get a tip-off on.

135
00:08:48,182 --> 00:08:50,142
That's why we have Team Three.

136
00:08:50,225 --> 00:08:52,019
Team One and Two
do all the important stuff

137
00:08:52,102 --> 00:08:53,896
and Team Three
gets the trivial stuff.

138
00:08:54,271 --> 00:08:55,731
They go on stakeouts

139
00:08:55,814 --> 00:08:58,650
to see how long people smoke
and poop during work hours.

140
00:08:58,734 --> 00:09:00,611
Once I saw them go around
all the break rooms

141
00:09:00,694 --> 00:09:02,571
to count the coffee mix packets.

142
00:09:03,530 --> 00:09:04,740
That's so depressing.

143
00:09:05,199 --> 00:09:07,117
People think our Audit Team
is powerful enough

144
00:09:07,201 --> 00:09:08,577
to bring down birds from the sky.

145
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:10,996
- Team Three...
- Not Team Three.

146
00:09:11,538 --> 00:09:13,373
They're more like poop-scoops.

147
00:09:14,333 --> 00:09:15,793
I like the ring of that. Poop-scoops.

148
00:09:18,212 --> 00:09:19,797
What if someone were to hear you?

149
00:09:20,422 --> 00:09:21,423
It's Executive Assistant Park.

150
00:09:29,223 --> 00:09:30,349
- Gosh.
- My word.

151
00:09:30,432 --> 00:09:32,726
Hello, Ms. Park.
Isn't it a lovely day?

152
00:09:34,770 --> 00:09:35,854
It is.

153
00:09:37,147 --> 00:09:38,899
We got to see her before work.

154
00:09:38,982 --> 00:09:40,776
I have a good feeling about today.

155
00:09:41,819 --> 00:09:43,362
I'll go ahead.
You guys finish breakfast.

156
00:09:43,654 --> 00:09:45,155
What? You're going already?

157
00:10:07,302 --> 00:10:08,887
What's my afternoon schedule?

158
00:10:09,638 --> 00:10:11,932
You have a meeting
with Haemu Media's executives.

159
00:10:20,983 --> 00:10:22,192
I like your tie.

160
00:10:28,407 --> 00:10:29,992
You have a good eye, sir.

161
00:11:06,987 --> 00:11:08,363
- Ki-jun.
- Hey.

162
00:11:24,087 --> 00:11:25,130
Ki-jun.

163
00:11:25,589 --> 00:11:27,758
Our team saw the PR clip,
and everyone's raving

164
00:11:27,841 --> 00:11:29,676
and wondering who you are.

165
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:32,596
Really? They'll swoon
if they see me in person.

166
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:35,766
What are you doing today after work?

167
00:11:36,183 --> 00:11:37,267
How about a drink?

168
00:11:37,351 --> 00:11:39,770
I heard a nice wine bar
opened nearby.

169
00:11:40,229 --> 00:11:42,314
- Where is it?
- It's called...

170
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:55,118
I'll be in touch, okay?

171
00:11:55,202 --> 00:11:56,370
Wait, Ki-jun.

172
00:11:57,287 --> 00:11:58,872
14TH FLOOR
PLANNING TEAM, AUDIT TEAM

173
00:12:07,297 --> 00:12:08,382
What the heck?

174
00:12:15,555 --> 00:12:16,598
Ji-hye...

175
00:12:19,476 --> 00:12:21,853
That's way too passionate a greeting
after a long break.

176
00:12:23,272 --> 00:12:24,648
I missed you.

177
00:12:25,816 --> 00:12:27,401
Will you meet up
with that other girl later?

178
00:12:27,734 --> 00:12:28,777
Hang out with me.

179
00:12:31,154 --> 00:12:33,198
No, wait. What?

180
00:12:36,368 --> 00:12:37,494
Aren't you getting married?

181
00:12:38,870 --> 00:12:39,913
You called it off?

182
00:12:39,997 --> 00:12:40,998
Not exactly.

183
00:12:41,873 --> 00:12:43,208
I feel a bit down.

184
00:12:43,959 --> 00:12:47,462
The idea that I'll be stuck
with one guy for the rest of my life.

185
00:12:50,299 --> 00:12:51,383
How about

186
00:12:52,634 --> 00:12:55,512
we have a good time
just one last time?

187
00:13:02,394 --> 00:13:03,687
I'm not that kind of guy.

188
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:16,033
It's natural to feel uneasy
before the wedding.

189
00:13:17,534 --> 00:13:18,785
I'll entertain you instead.

190
00:13:19,786 --> 00:13:21,288
With a hefty cash envelope.

191
00:13:21,913 --> 00:13:23,957
What the heck is that?

192
00:13:24,624 --> 00:13:26,126
How much will you gift me?

193
00:13:33,091 --> 00:13:34,092
Hey.

194
00:13:54,279 --> 00:13:56,656
- What are you doing?
- Hey, Mr. Noh.

195
00:13:56,907 --> 00:13:58,200
Look at that. It's in bloom.

196
00:13:58,617 --> 00:14:00,494
I wonder who's watering
and looking after it.

197
00:14:00,786 --> 00:14:03,455
It's doing so well
in this desolate place.

198
00:14:03,705 --> 00:14:05,707
Gosh, you're very sentimental.

199
00:14:05,791 --> 00:14:07,667
I'm sure you don't care.

200
00:14:07,751 --> 00:14:10,212
Because your life's in full bloom.

201
00:14:10,295 --> 00:14:12,172
Ms. Hong from HR just told me.

202
00:14:13,215 --> 00:14:15,509
You might get a special promotion
for catching Director Kang.

203
00:14:15,592 --> 00:14:16,635
Is that true?

204
00:14:18,136 --> 00:14:21,348
- I can't say.
- Wait a minute. I guess it's true.

205
00:14:21,932 --> 00:14:25,644
You were Director Kim's favorite
when he was Head of Audit.

206
00:14:27,896 --> 00:14:30,273
I trust you'll look out for me
later on.

207
00:14:30,357 --> 00:14:31,483
Don't forget that, okay?

208
00:14:32,359 --> 00:14:35,112
Guys, have you heard the news?

209
00:14:35,737 --> 00:14:36,738
What news?

210
00:14:36,822 --> 00:14:38,365
People are losing their minds
here and there.

211
00:14:38,448 --> 00:14:40,117
A really scary rumor is going around.

212
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,743
It's code red right now.

213
00:14:41,827 --> 00:14:42,828
What's going on?

214
00:14:44,913 --> 00:14:45,914
Joo In-a

215
00:14:46,790 --> 00:14:47,833
<i>is back.</i>

216
00:14:50,001 --> 00:14:51,002
Isn't that Joo In-a?

217
00:14:51,086 --> 00:14:52,421
- For real?
- It really is her.

218
00:14:52,879 --> 00:14:54,131
HAEMU INTRANET
1 NEW MESSAGE FROM MR. KIM

219
00:14:55,090 --> 00:14:56,466
She must be back.

220
00:14:56,550 --> 00:14:57,676
NEW MESSAGE
NEW NOTIFICATION

221
00:14:57,759 --> 00:14:59,344
What's going on?

222
00:14:59,428 --> 00:15:00,554
YOU GOT A NEW MESSAGE

223
00:15:00,637 --> 00:15:01,638
She actually came back.

224
00:15:02,722 --> 00:15:04,474
- What's happening?
- What do you think?

225
00:15:05,892 --> 00:15:07,144
<i>- Joo In-a's here.
- Joo's here.</i>

226
00:15:07,227 --> 00:15:09,146
<i>- We're done for.
- Is she back for good?</i>

227
00:15:09,229 --> 00:15:10,689
<i>- What a disaster.
- I'll be damned.</i>

228
00:15:11,898 --> 00:15:13,358
I HATE GETTING CC-ED TO EMAILS

229
00:15:13,442 --> 00:15:14,443
WILL OVERSEAS BRANCHES SUFFER?

230
00:15:14,526 --> 00:15:15,569
ALL SITES ARE ON STANDBY

231
00:15:15,652 --> 00:15:16,695
HOW WILL THIS CHANGE THINGS?

232
00:15:16,778 --> 00:15:17,946
I WONDER IF THE EXECUTIVES ARE AFRAID

233
00:15:18,572 --> 00:15:19,823
<i>You know, at work</i>

234
00:15:20,198 --> 00:15:22,117
<i>you must beware
of those with nicknames.</i>

235
00:15:23,118 --> 00:15:26,246
People give nicknames
to badmouth freely.

236
00:15:27,914 --> 00:15:29,875
I bet Joo In-a has

237
00:15:30,834 --> 00:15:32,252
a dozen or so nicknames.

238
00:15:32,961 --> 00:15:35,380
<i>"</i>Joo In-Out" is a famous one.

239
00:15:35,881 --> 00:15:39,342
<i>Get on her bad side and you're out.</i>

240
00:15:39,926 --> 00:15:42,345
<i>I thought that was funny.
"Joo-tergeist."</i>

241
00:15:42,721 --> 00:15:45,891
<i>She's like a poltergeist
that stays at work day and night.</i>

242
00:15:46,808 --> 00:15:49,269
<i>I heard she earned a new nickname</i>

243
00:15:49,352 --> 00:15:51,521
<i>- while working overseas.
- What's that?</i>

244
00:15:51,855 --> 00:15:54,316
<i>She fought a gang
over a business license.</i>

245
00:15:56,818 --> 00:15:57,819
<i>They called her</i>

246
00:15:59,696 --> 00:16:00,780
<i>"Joo-sniper."</i>

247
00:16:02,199 --> 00:16:04,242
She actually fired a gun?

248
00:16:04,326 --> 00:16:05,452
I'm sure it's just a rumor.

249
00:16:05,535 --> 00:16:07,996
How could something like that
even become a rumor?

250
00:16:08,288 --> 00:16:09,831
What's most important is

251
00:16:11,166 --> 00:16:13,084
which division she'll join.

252
00:16:14,002 --> 00:16:15,045
Don't you think?

253
00:16:27,974 --> 00:16:28,975
JOO'S IN THE ELEVATOR

254
00:16:29,476 --> 00:16:33,063
KIM JIN-HEE FROM PLANNING:
JOO'S IN THE ELEVATOR

255
00:16:33,897 --> 00:16:35,023
She's in the elevator.

256
00:16:35,106 --> 00:16:36,149
Which floor did she press?

257
00:16:36,483 --> 00:16:37,859
JOO'S IN THE ELEVATOR

258
00:16:37,943 --> 00:16:40,820
WHICH FLOOR DID SHE PRESS?

259
00:16:43,949 --> 00:16:45,825
<i>She's smashing the Close Door button.</i>

260
00:16:45,909 --> 00:16:48,870
<i>I think my heart
is getting smashed, too.</i>

261
00:16:50,413 --> 00:16:51,581
<i>Passed the fourth floor.</i>

262
00:16:54,334 --> 00:16:55,335
<i>Fifth floor.</i>

263
00:16:55,835 --> 00:16:57,128
Passed the sixth floor!

264
00:17:00,423 --> 00:17:02,050
Where the heck is she going?

265
00:17:02,384 --> 00:17:03,635
Did HR post a notice?

266
00:17:03,718 --> 00:17:04,886
No, not yet.

267
00:17:04,970 --> 00:17:06,304
HR AND INFORMATION OFFICE

268
00:17:07,639 --> 00:17:09,599
HEAD OF HR, HAEMU GROUP
BOO SE-YOUNG

269
00:17:15,397 --> 00:17:17,607
WOULD YOU LIKE TO PROCEED?

270
00:17:17,691 --> 00:17:19,568
APPROVAL OF APPOINTMENT,
JOO IN-A, DEPARTMENT HEAD

271
00:17:19,651 --> 00:17:20,652
CANCEL

272
00:17:20,735 --> 00:17:21,736
APPROVE

273
00:17:24,406 --> 00:17:25,407
<i>Ninth floor.</i>

274
00:17:28,660 --> 00:17:29,703
Tenth floor.

275
00:17:29,786 --> 00:17:31,371
Why does she keep coming up?

276
00:17:32,122 --> 00:17:33,957
AS LONG AS
SHE DOESN'T GET OFF WITH ME

277
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:35,959
JOO IN-A, PLEASE GET OFF
WHY'S THE ELEVATOR SO SLOW TODAY?

278
00:17:38,169 --> 00:17:39,170
PHEW, I'M GETTING OFF FIRST

279
00:17:39,254 --> 00:17:40,255
I'M SO JEALOUS

280
00:17:42,215 --> 00:17:43,425
PASSED 13TH FLOOR

281
00:17:43,508 --> 00:17:45,093
WILL SHE GET OFF HERE?

282
00:17:45,176 --> 00:17:46,386
14TH FLOOR...

283
00:18:15,165 --> 00:18:16,207
It's the 14th floor!

284
00:18:25,842 --> 00:18:27,135
<i>Stay calm, everyone!</i>

285
00:18:27,469 --> 00:18:30,013
<i>The Planning Office is
on the 14th floor, too.</i>

286
00:18:31,014 --> 00:18:32,223
PLANNING OFFICE

287
00:18:32,474 --> 00:18:33,475
Put everything away.

288
00:18:33,558 --> 00:18:36,269
Hey, get rid of all the dust.
Wipe every single speck.

289
00:18:36,353 --> 00:18:38,355
Dump all the documents
and scrap papers on your desk.

290
00:18:38,438 --> 00:18:41,775
And your coffees!
Drink it up and dump the cups.

291
00:19:07,217 --> 00:19:08,760
Is there a Kim Gyu-yeong?

292
00:19:12,806 --> 00:19:14,599
ONE-DAY COURIER

293
00:19:15,350 --> 00:19:16,476
What are you doing to me?

294
00:19:23,608 --> 00:19:24,609
It's nice to meet you all.

295
00:19:25,026 --> 00:19:27,278
I'm Joo In-a, the new Head of Audit.

296
00:19:35,036 --> 00:19:37,914
Come on, now.
Why the dull atmosphere?

297
00:19:38,289 --> 00:19:40,083
How about I sing a song
to lighten things up?

298
00:19:47,090 --> 00:19:49,592
Thank you for the warm welcome.

299
00:19:51,094 --> 00:19:52,095
Nice to meet you.

300
00:19:52,637 --> 00:19:54,222
Manager Kwon Myeong-jin.

301
00:19:54,305 --> 00:19:55,640
Yes. I'm pleased to meet you.

302
00:19:56,683 --> 00:19:58,309
You sound overly pleased. Relax.

303
00:19:58,393 --> 00:19:59,811
I will. Sorry.

304
00:19:59,894 --> 00:20:02,021
I'm Mun Gyeong-jin,
assistant team leader of Team One.

305
00:20:02,439 --> 00:20:03,773
You're an assistant team leader?

306
00:20:04,107 --> 00:20:06,526
You look young for that title.
I hope we get on well.

307
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:09,195
I'm Kim Tae-hwan,
Leader of Audit Team Two.

308
00:20:09,279 --> 00:20:11,364
- I hope we can work well.
- I really hope so.

309
00:20:11,448 --> 00:20:12,574
Let's try to get along.

310
00:20:13,408 --> 00:20:15,785
Jeong Dong-min,
assistant team leader of Team Two.

311
00:20:16,119 --> 00:20:17,120
I hope we get along.

312
00:20:17,662 --> 00:20:19,914
I'm Ju Yeon-u,
senior associate of Team One.

313
00:20:20,832 --> 00:20:23,168
Which Ju clan
does your surname belong to?

314
00:20:23,543 --> 00:20:24,544
Well...

315
00:20:24,794 --> 00:20:25,795
Is it from the word "juice"?

316
00:20:26,171 --> 00:20:27,589
Yes, you're right.

317
00:20:29,299 --> 00:20:30,550
I hope we get along.

318
00:20:31,092 --> 00:20:32,719
Wait, she's pretty normal.

319
00:20:32,844 --> 00:20:35,013
There are too many groundless rumors.

320
00:20:35,346 --> 00:20:37,474
Right. We got scared for no reason.

321
00:20:39,309 --> 00:20:40,351
Hello.

322
00:20:40,435 --> 00:20:42,604
I'm Sung Doo-gi,
a senior associate on Team One.

323
00:20:42,687 --> 00:20:43,730
I hope we work well together!

324
00:20:43,897 --> 00:20:45,148
I love your energy.

325
00:20:45,398 --> 00:20:47,358
- Let's work well together.
- Thank you.

326
00:20:47,442 --> 00:20:49,068
I'm Assistant Manager Ahn Min-su
from the same team.

327
00:20:49,152 --> 00:20:50,278
I hope to impress you.

328
00:20:51,237 --> 00:20:52,781
I look forward
to your impressive work.

329
00:20:53,198 --> 00:20:54,240
Thank you.

330
00:20:57,744 --> 00:20:59,871
Hello, I'm Assistant Manager
Noh Ki-jun of Audit Team One.

331
00:21:02,916 --> 00:21:04,417
Assistant Manager Noh Ki-jun.

332
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:21,643
Shall we get to work?

333
00:21:30,693 --> 00:21:32,445
Excuse me, Ms. Joo?

334
00:21:32,862 --> 00:21:34,364
I'm sorry to bother you
when you just came in.

335
00:21:34,948 --> 00:21:36,825
No problem. Give that to me.

336
00:21:42,705 --> 00:21:44,707
It's a routine audit notification.

337
00:21:44,791 --> 00:21:47,418
I need to send it right away.
Please approve it for me.

338
00:21:47,836 --> 00:21:49,170
Haemu Industries.

339
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:50,839
You've audited them
for five years in a row.

340
00:21:50,922 --> 00:21:51,923
Yes, that's right.

341
00:21:52,590 --> 00:21:56,177
I've been in charge since my transfer
here from Haemu Industries.

342
00:21:56,261 --> 00:21:58,429
You've been auditing
your former boss for five years.

343
00:21:58,513 --> 00:21:59,514
Yes.

344
00:22:01,599 --> 00:22:03,476
You can stop now.
It must be boring for both parties.

345
00:22:05,103 --> 00:22:06,688
Our new rule that is no one audits

346
00:22:06,771 --> 00:22:08,731
the same subsidiary
for more than two years.

347
00:22:08,815 --> 00:22:10,650
One year if you used to work there.

348
00:22:14,571 --> 00:22:18,074
I get what you're saying, Ms. Joo.

349
00:22:18,908 --> 00:22:21,536
I know better than anyone
how they do business.

350
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:24,539
I also know
which areas are usually corrupt.

351
00:22:25,999 --> 00:22:27,876
How corrupt is that place
that you couldn't

352
00:22:28,293 --> 00:22:30,086
get to the bottom of it
for five years?

353
00:22:30,587 --> 00:22:31,796
Pardon?

354
00:22:34,966 --> 00:22:36,342
Well, Ms. Joo.

355
00:22:36,968 --> 00:22:38,511
- What I mean is...
- You laughed?

356
00:22:50,815 --> 00:22:52,358
I told you to stop going.

357
00:22:53,610 --> 00:22:55,153
That's all you have to do.

358
00:22:56,195 --> 00:22:57,780
Why do you talk back at every turn?

359
00:22:57,989 --> 00:23:01,034
Do you think I'm here to have
a lengthy discussion with you?

360
00:23:02,201 --> 00:23:04,621
If you know
about Haemu Industries that well

361
00:23:04,954 --> 00:23:06,706
why did you only do
a brief look-over every year?

362
00:23:07,206 --> 00:23:09,167
You haven't found anything
that led to disciplinary action.

363
00:23:10,251 --> 00:23:12,378
You worked there for over ten years.

364
00:23:12,462 --> 00:23:14,297
You just couldn't bear
to punish anyone.

365
00:23:14,380 --> 00:23:16,132
No, it's not that at all.

366
00:23:16,215 --> 00:23:19,636
Then did you collude with them
to hide a sweet slush fund somewhere?

367
00:23:20,011 --> 00:23:21,220
Shall I go digging myself?

368
00:23:21,429 --> 00:23:23,681
To see if you audited them
or did business with them?

369
00:23:23,765 --> 00:23:25,600
Why would you
suggest something so dreadful?

370
00:23:25,683 --> 00:23:26,726
If that's not it...

371
00:23:27,894 --> 00:23:29,896
You probably don't take me seriously.

372
00:23:31,105 --> 00:23:32,482
I apologize.

373
00:23:47,914 --> 00:23:49,207
Don't you have any work to do?

374
00:23:54,796 --> 00:23:58,549
I'll speak with each of you
in a one-on-one meeting.

375
00:23:58,633 --> 00:24:00,760
Come to the interview room
when I call your name.

376
00:24:08,893 --> 00:24:10,478
MUN GYEONG-JIN,
CALCULATE SEVERANCE PAY

377
00:24:10,561 --> 00:24:12,188
HOW MUCH TO OPEN
A FRIED CHICKEN STORE?

378
00:24:12,271 --> 00:24:15,274
SHOULD I QUIT?

379
00:24:15,358 --> 00:24:17,110
I WANT TO CRY

380
00:24:17,193 --> 00:24:19,696
INTERVIEW ROOM

381
00:24:30,123 --> 00:24:31,791
Manager Ha Jin-u of Team Two.

382
00:24:42,343 --> 00:24:44,012
It turned into Jurassic Park
in an instant.

383
00:24:45,930 --> 00:24:47,974
Hey, how can you work right now?

384
00:24:48,057 --> 00:24:50,476
Why not? She had a point.

385
00:24:51,561 --> 00:24:53,521
Do specially promoted people
have something in common?

386
00:24:53,604 --> 00:24:55,314
I heard she got promoted three times.

387
00:24:57,734 --> 00:25:00,069
You want to audit
Haemu Pharmaceuticals again?

388
00:25:01,070 --> 00:25:02,739
You're working on something,
aren't you?

389
00:25:03,114 --> 00:25:05,074
What is it? What are they up to?

390
00:25:06,659 --> 00:25:09,120
When I have them
right where I want them

391
00:25:10,371 --> 00:25:11,456
I'll tell you then.

392
00:25:12,248 --> 00:25:13,833
You special promotion jerks.

393
00:25:24,635 --> 00:25:26,471
Can someone get Mr. Ha
a cup of water?

394
00:25:26,763 --> 00:25:27,805
Yes, ma'am.

395
00:25:30,516 --> 00:25:32,018
- I'm useless.
- No, you're not.

396
00:25:43,237 --> 00:25:44,906
Assistant Manager Noh Ki-jun
of Team One?

397
00:25:46,991 --> 00:25:48,034
Okay.

398
00:25:54,807 --> 00:25:56,809
Our meeting will only
last three minutes.

399
00:25:57,727 --> 00:26:00,188
Good. I'm all for efficient meetings.

400
00:26:01,814 --> 00:26:04,025
Let's see, Assistant Manager Noh.

401
00:26:05,318 --> 00:26:06,653
A pretty favorable evaluation.

402
00:26:06,736 --> 00:26:08,821
You've received top evaluations
ever since you joined Haemu.

403
00:26:09,447 --> 00:26:12,700
- I was lucky.
- So it was all luck.

404
00:26:15,286 --> 00:26:18,289
You've handled only the biggest cases
in each subsidiary.

405
00:26:19,207 --> 00:26:20,833
You closed a lot of big ones.

406
00:26:21,251 --> 00:26:22,293
Yes, my luck

407
00:26:23,002 --> 00:26:24,587
followed as I worked hard.

408
00:26:25,505 --> 00:26:28,258
Let's make a minor change
to your role, Mr. Noh.

409
00:26:29,259 --> 00:26:30,301
<i>A special promotion?</i>

410
00:26:31,010 --> 00:26:32,053
<i>Already?</i>

411
00:26:32,637 --> 00:26:34,931
It's not
personnel evaluation season yet.

412
00:26:35,014 --> 00:26:36,266
That doesn't matter.

413
00:26:36,349 --> 00:26:38,685
Well, if that's what you want,
I'll willingly accept...

414
00:26:38,768 --> 00:26:40,228
I'm sending you to Team Three.

415
00:26:41,062 --> 00:26:42,188
What? To Team Three?

416
00:26:42,272 --> 00:26:45,024
You'll transfer to Team Three
and take over the PM cases.

417
00:26:45,400 --> 00:26:47,569
- "PM" is our code for...
- Personal misconduct.

418
00:26:47,902 --> 00:26:50,488
P for personal and M for misconduct.

419
00:26:50,947 --> 00:26:52,240
They're mostly workplace affairs.

420
00:26:52,865 --> 00:26:54,534
You want me to handle
office scandals?

421
00:26:55,827 --> 00:26:56,828
Yes.

422
00:27:00,164 --> 00:27:02,333
Okay, then. That means

423
00:27:03,501 --> 00:27:04,502
today is your new day one.

424
00:27:11,884 --> 00:27:15,013
Ms. Joo, how could you send me
to Team Three to investigate affairs?

425
00:27:15,305 --> 00:27:16,431
I can't understand why.

426
00:27:17,307 --> 00:27:19,100
Why should I help you understand?

427
00:27:19,434 --> 00:27:20,852
I exercised my right
as your superior.

428
00:27:20,935 --> 00:27:23,187
Yes, that's true. But you admitted

429
00:27:23,271 --> 00:27:24,814
that I performed well every year.

430
00:27:26,816 --> 00:27:27,859
You did great.

431
00:27:30,653 --> 00:27:31,654
He's joining us?

432
00:27:32,322 --> 00:27:34,157
I was going to inform you
when things got underway.

433
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:35,950
I'm working on something
with my team.

434
00:27:36,409 --> 00:27:39,120
It's an important audit
on one of our subsidiaries.

435
00:27:39,203 --> 00:27:40,371
Let me finish it.

436
00:27:40,455 --> 00:27:42,665
Put all the info on our cloud server.

437
00:27:42,749 --> 00:27:44,334
I'll take a look
and allocate someone else.

438
00:27:45,084 --> 00:27:47,795
It follows a complicated logic
and involves many executives.

439
00:27:47,879 --> 00:27:50,340
It requires a very subtle approach.

440
00:27:51,549 --> 00:27:52,675
The only one for the job?

441
00:27:55,428 --> 00:27:56,554
That would be me.

442
00:28:17,033 --> 00:28:18,284
Gosh, this is fun.

443
00:28:20,828 --> 00:28:22,830
Mr. Noh, are you that special?

444
00:28:23,039 --> 00:28:24,499
Do you have some kind of superpower?

445
00:28:24,582 --> 00:28:26,209
Can you fly or teleport?

446
00:28:26,292 --> 00:28:27,377
Can you do the palm blast?

447
00:28:28,252 --> 00:28:29,879
Who do you think you are

448
00:28:29,962 --> 00:28:32,215
that you would be the only person
who can do this particular job?

449
00:28:33,800 --> 00:28:34,884
No way.

450
00:28:35,301 --> 00:28:38,346
Do you actually believe
some employees are irreplaceable?

451
00:28:38,888 --> 00:28:40,807
Apple's doing just fine
after Steve Jobs died.

452
00:28:41,182 --> 00:28:43,017
Do you think
a project will collapse without you?

453
00:28:43,101 --> 00:28:44,227
Audit Team 1, of all teams?

454
00:28:46,020 --> 00:28:48,189
How could you be so utterly naive?

455
00:28:48,606 --> 00:28:50,024
Okay, let's say you were mistaken.

456
00:28:50,525 --> 00:28:53,736
How could you voice that to me?

457
00:28:54,404 --> 00:28:55,446
That's plain arrogance.

458
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:00,618
I'll let you off today
for making me laugh.

459
00:29:00,868 --> 00:29:02,453
Don't go overtime next time.

460
00:29:05,790 --> 00:29:07,250
Give me a reason, at least.

461
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:11,921
There must be a reason you want me
to handle affairs.

462
00:29:13,798 --> 00:29:14,841
It's because

463
00:29:15,174 --> 00:29:16,175
you are...

464
00:29:19,178 --> 00:29:20,638
the best one for the job.

465
00:29:29,063 --> 00:29:30,732
Hey, what happened?

466
00:29:31,232 --> 00:29:33,025
I thought she was
going to promote you.

467
00:29:33,109 --> 00:29:34,986
Forget the promotion.
This is more like a demotion.

468
00:29:35,862 --> 00:29:38,990
He's going to Team Three
to investigate affairs of all things.

469
00:29:39,490 --> 00:29:40,533
Still.

470
00:29:40,950 --> 00:29:42,618
They're all nice people.

471
00:29:43,119 --> 00:29:46,873
That's true.
Everyone on Team Three is nice.

472
00:29:47,749 --> 00:29:49,375
Do you need help with anything?

473
00:29:52,754 --> 00:29:54,964
- Do you need help?
- They seem nice.

474
00:29:55,423 --> 00:29:57,049
You'll do fine wherever you go.

475
00:30:02,597 --> 00:30:05,683
Assistant Manager Noh Ki-jun,
the ace of the Audit Team.

476
00:30:06,309 --> 00:30:07,518
Welcome.

477
00:30:07,602 --> 00:30:09,562
How old are you, Mr. Noh?

478
00:30:09,645 --> 00:30:11,439
Still not married?
Or haven't been able to?

479
00:30:12,064 --> 00:30:13,775
<i>The one man here
who gave up on any promotions.</i>

480
00:30:14,066 --> 00:30:15,359
<i>Team Leader Moo Kwang-il.</i>

481
00:30:15,443 --> 00:30:17,403
I heard that people
are reluctant to marry these days.

482
00:30:18,362 --> 00:30:20,865
Consider that a welcome kit.

483
00:30:21,115 --> 00:30:22,158
Look inside.

484
00:30:22,492 --> 00:30:25,578
<i>Bookkeeper Pyun Hae-young
who keeps the team going.</i>

485
00:30:26,829 --> 00:30:28,247
Everything you need is in there.

486
00:30:28,915 --> 00:30:31,042
We usually only give you two pens

487
00:30:31,125 --> 00:30:32,919
but I added one more
out of pity for you.

488
00:30:33,252 --> 00:30:35,129
Once you run out of ink
and need a replacement

489
00:30:35,213 --> 00:30:38,257
you must sign the ledger
before getting a new pen.

490
00:30:38,382 --> 00:30:41,010
Why would you go to such lengths
at a company as big as Haemu?

491
00:30:41,093 --> 00:30:42,178
If you don't like it

492
00:30:43,221 --> 00:30:44,806
blame that fool over there.

493
00:30:45,389 --> 00:30:48,851
You're taking it too far
when all I did was take batteries.

494
00:30:48,935 --> 00:30:51,354
You took a whole pack.

495
00:30:51,437 --> 00:30:54,440
A pack of size AA and AAA each.

496
00:30:55,233 --> 00:30:57,568
<i>The guy is always on the lookout
for things to steal</i>

497
00:30:57,985 --> 00:30:59,111
<i>Manager Cha Sung-tae.</i>

498
00:30:59,362 --> 00:31:00,404
Darn it.

499
00:31:00,988 --> 00:31:02,114
Excuse me, Mr. Noh.

500
00:31:02,198 --> 00:31:04,367
Welcome to Team Three.

501
00:31:04,659 --> 00:31:06,369
If there's anything
you need help with

502
00:31:06,452 --> 00:31:08,079
you can come to me at any time.

503
00:31:08,162 --> 00:31:10,373
<i>Senior Associate Baek Hyun-kyu,
who thinks he's a troubleshooter.</i>

504
00:31:10,456 --> 00:31:11,999
<i>He's called "White Blood Cell"
for some reason.</i>

505
00:31:12,083 --> 00:31:15,002
Oh, and before you sit down,
let me adjust your chair for you.

506
00:31:25,763 --> 00:31:28,432
<i>Right! Assistant Manager Yoon Da-yae
is a part of this team.</i>

507
00:31:29,183 --> 00:31:30,601
<i>An SNU graduate with a certified CPA.</i>

508
00:31:30,685 --> 00:31:32,019
<i>The one with crazy credentials!</i>

509
00:31:33,938 --> 00:31:35,439
Hello, Ms. Yoon.

510
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:38,901
Ms. Yoon has that Gen Z attitude.

511
00:31:39,527 --> 00:31:40,570
You know what Gen Z is, right?

512
00:31:42,363 --> 00:31:43,447
You can't talk to her.

513
00:31:48,828 --> 00:31:51,706
<i>What in the world is nice
about this team?</i>

514
00:31:53,583 --> 00:31:54,667
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

515
00:31:55,376 --> 00:31:56,544
- Stop it, Manager.
<i>- I...</i>

516
00:31:56,627 --> 00:31:57,920
- That's crazy.
- What did I do?

517
00:31:58,004 --> 00:31:59,005
<i>I...</i>

518
00:31:59,755 --> 00:32:01,716
<i>I can't believe
I'm a part of this team!</i>

519
00:32:02,466 --> 00:32:04,468
Even her parents can't talk to her.

520
00:32:04,552 --> 00:32:05,845
- Why did you take this?
- Quiet.

521
00:32:27,992 --> 00:32:29,577
Dinner's ready.

522
00:32:34,457 --> 00:32:36,125
Will he be late again?

523
00:32:39,670 --> 00:32:41,005
HUBBY

524
00:32:48,095 --> 00:32:50,723
<i>Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.</i>

525
00:32:50,806 --> 00:32:53,059
<i>You will be charged after the beep.</i>

526
00:32:59,231 --> 00:33:01,734
WIFEY

527
00:33:04,195 --> 00:33:05,196
Yes?

528
00:33:05,404 --> 00:33:06,656
Yes, I understand. Goodbye.

529
00:33:07,615 --> 00:33:09,450
- How did it go?
- I talked to them.

530
00:33:09,533 --> 00:33:11,452
- They'll meet the deadline.
- Yes!

531
00:33:11,535 --> 00:33:13,204
Nice job.

532
00:33:13,287 --> 00:33:14,830
You've become good
at pressing the vendors now.

533
00:33:14,914 --> 00:33:16,040
It's all thanks to my teacher.

534
00:33:17,500 --> 00:33:18,668
You're getting a call.

535
00:33:22,546 --> 00:33:23,589
Hey, honey. Yes?

536
00:33:24,757 --> 00:33:26,550
Did I forget to mention?
I have a team dinner tonight.

537
00:33:29,053 --> 00:33:30,763
You're having another team dinner?

538
00:33:30,846 --> 00:33:32,348
Yes, I'm sorry. I've been busy.

539
00:33:32,431 --> 00:33:35,851
Hello, ma'am.
It's Jeong Mi-young speaking.

540
00:33:36,769 --> 00:33:38,729
Yes, hello.

541
00:33:38,938 --> 00:33:40,773
It's been a while
since your husband went home early.

542
00:33:40,856 --> 00:33:42,483
We've been too busy
with the task force.

543
00:33:42,733 --> 00:33:45,528
I'll let him leave
as early as possible today.

544
00:33:47,363 --> 00:33:49,240
Hey, honey.
I'll be home early. I'm sorry.

545
00:33:49,824 --> 00:33:52,410
Okay, don't be too late.

546
00:33:52,868 --> 00:33:53,869
Bye.

547
00:33:56,956 --> 00:33:58,165
Jeez.

548
00:34:06,924 --> 00:34:09,927
Who does she think she is
to let my husband go early?

549
00:34:12,054 --> 00:34:13,139
Darn it.

550
00:34:15,307 --> 00:34:16,350
How dare she?

551
00:34:18,394 --> 00:34:19,562
Who does she think she is?

552
00:34:23,315 --> 00:34:24,316
Damn it.

553
00:34:26,652 --> 00:34:28,154
I've had enough.

554
00:34:33,284 --> 00:34:34,285
Mr. Noh.

555
00:34:34,744 --> 00:34:36,746
These four seats are
the tip-off lines.

556
00:34:36,829 --> 00:34:38,706
You'll get lots of calls

557
00:34:39,165 --> 00:34:40,332
so pick up and accept the reports.

558
00:34:43,669 --> 00:34:45,171
- Yes, okay.
- Okay.

559
00:34:55,931 --> 00:34:57,099
You've reached Audit Team One...

560
00:34:58,476 --> 00:34:59,852
No, Audit Team Three.

561
00:34:59,935 --> 00:35:00,978
<i>Hello.</i>

562
00:35:01,312 --> 00:35:03,272
<i>I'm not sure
if I should be bringing this up</i>

563
00:35:03,731 --> 00:35:05,816
<i>but I'm calling
regarding my team leader.</i>

564
00:35:07,568 --> 00:35:09,195
Yes, I see.

565
00:35:09,278 --> 00:35:11,363
Are you looking
to make an internal report?

566
00:35:11,614 --> 00:35:14,825
<i>I mean, my team leader
keeps farting in the office.</i>

567
00:35:15,076 --> 00:35:17,661
<i>It's a bit too much
to hear it go off all day.</i>

568
00:35:17,745 --> 00:35:19,789
<i>It's the worst office environment!</i>

569
00:35:19,872 --> 00:35:21,832
<i>At least give us an air purifier.</i>

570
00:35:22,666 --> 00:35:23,834
I see.

571
00:35:25,586 --> 00:35:27,004
So your team leader farts?

572
00:35:41,143 --> 00:35:42,269
You've reached Audit Team...

573
00:35:42,853 --> 00:35:45,981
<i>You damn asshole!
What took you so long to pick up?</i>

574
00:35:46,107 --> 00:35:48,734
<i>Yet you get paid a fortune,
don't you, you punk?</i>

575
00:35:48,818 --> 00:35:50,694
- ...Three.
<i>- What Three?</i>

576
00:35:50,778 --> 00:35:52,905
<i>You'll only get a grip
when that business goes down!</i>

577
00:35:52,988 --> 00:35:55,157
<i>- Does your company know you do that?</i>
- Sure.

578
00:35:56,450 --> 00:35:58,202
- What would you like to report?
<i>- Report, my ass!</i>

579
00:35:58,285 --> 00:35:59,745
<i>I'll report your damn life!</i>

580
00:35:59,829 --> 00:36:00,830
<i>What's your name?</i>

581
00:36:00,913 --> 00:36:03,165
<i>I'll talk to your chairman
and tell him all about you!</i>

582
00:36:03,249 --> 00:36:04,917
<i>What the heck is your name?</i>

583
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,293
<i>What's your name?</i>

584
00:36:11,382 --> 00:36:12,967
What are these?

585
00:36:13,050 --> 00:36:14,718
Evidence of infidelity!

586
00:36:15,010 --> 00:36:18,430
I had to go through the trash can
to retrieve those.

587
00:36:18,639 --> 00:36:20,057
Yes, so what are...

588
00:36:28,816 --> 00:36:30,442
Where are you going?

589
00:36:58,554 --> 00:36:59,597
Jeez.

590
00:37:10,399 --> 00:37:12,526
Mr. Noh, are you okay?

591
00:37:12,902 --> 00:37:14,945
You looked pale as you ran in.

592
00:37:16,113 --> 00:37:17,865
Is there anyone to pat your back?

593
00:37:18,490 --> 00:37:20,784
If not, I can always come in
for a second.

594
00:37:31,712 --> 00:37:32,880
I'm all right.

595
00:37:35,507 --> 00:37:37,134
Are you sure?

596
00:37:37,718 --> 00:37:40,346
You can take a break
if it's too tough for you.

597
00:37:41,096 --> 00:37:43,724
Nothing beats being healthy.

598
00:37:55,611 --> 00:37:57,446
Let's do proper introductions.

599
00:37:58,405 --> 00:38:01,200
The Head of Audit, Joo In-a.

600
00:38:02,534 --> 00:38:03,994
The former Head of Audit

601
00:38:04,078 --> 00:38:05,955
and the current Director
of Strategic Planning, Kim Han-su.

602
00:38:06,830 --> 00:38:07,957
I've heard a lot about you.

603
00:38:08,999 --> 00:38:10,084
Congratulations on your promotion.

604
00:38:11,627 --> 00:38:13,170
Head of HR, Boo Se-young.

605
00:38:13,921 --> 00:38:15,214
It's been a while, In-a.

606
00:38:17,383 --> 00:38:20,302
We used to work in the same team.

607
00:38:20,928 --> 00:38:21,971
But of course

608
00:38:22,680 --> 00:38:23,973
I started before her.

609
00:38:24,640 --> 00:38:25,849
Hey, Se-young.

610
00:38:26,308 --> 00:38:27,977
You're looking great.

611
00:38:28,310 --> 00:38:29,603
Things must be swell in HR.

612
00:38:33,482 --> 00:38:35,985
You two seem rather close.

613
00:38:36,735 --> 00:38:37,778
That's nice.

614
00:38:37,987 --> 00:38:41,657
This recent appointment was
a genius move, I must say.

615
00:38:42,324 --> 00:38:45,703
We can call our audit teams the sword

616
00:38:45,786 --> 00:38:48,289
of the vice president
and the president.

617
00:38:49,331 --> 00:38:51,917
Someone like Ms. Joo
would be perfect for the job.

618
00:38:52,751 --> 00:38:54,461
Oh, my. How did you know?

619
00:38:57,047 --> 00:38:58,299
I have a knack for swordsmanship.

620
00:39:01,635 --> 00:39:03,721
Ms. Joo has a witty sense of humor.

621
00:39:04,471 --> 00:39:06,015
You'll find it funny
once you get used to it.

622
00:39:08,517 --> 00:39:10,519
How does it feel breathing
the Seoul air again after so long?

623
00:39:10,602 --> 00:39:12,354
The air is the same everywhere.

624
00:39:13,439 --> 00:39:15,232
But the fine dust seems
to have worsened.

625
00:39:16,483 --> 00:39:17,526
So?

626
00:39:19,278 --> 00:39:21,488
Do you regret coming back?

627
00:39:29,872 --> 00:39:30,873
If I do

628
00:39:31,790 --> 00:39:33,208
do I have the option to go back?

629
00:39:51,643 --> 00:39:53,145
Look at the time.

630
00:39:53,604 --> 00:39:55,272
Why don't we grab some dinner...

631
00:39:55,356 --> 00:39:57,441
I have a lot of tasks
to figure out right now.

632
00:39:58,359 --> 00:39:59,401
Why don't we

633
00:40:00,194 --> 00:40:01,362
slice some steak next time?

634
00:40:01,445 --> 00:40:02,446
Yes, sure.

635
00:40:04,573 --> 00:40:05,616
Mr. Vice President.

636
00:40:06,116 --> 00:40:08,327
I'm eating with my parents tonight.

637
00:40:08,410 --> 00:40:09,620
My wife is probably there now.

638
00:40:10,371 --> 00:40:11,789
Goodness, Mr. Vice President.

639
00:40:12,373 --> 00:40:13,749
You're such a romantic.

640
00:40:15,501 --> 00:40:17,878
How's the president doing?

641
00:40:18,212 --> 00:40:19,922
He was discharged last week

642
00:40:20,297 --> 00:40:21,340
but we must keep an eye on him.

643
00:40:23,258 --> 00:40:25,803
I've been
checking his condition frequently.

644
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:25,779
<i>Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected...</i>

645
00:41:33,495 --> 00:41:35,706
<i>- Your call cannot be connected...</i>
- Darn it.

646
00:41:40,085 --> 00:41:41,587
WHY AREN'T YOU ANSWERING MY CALL?
PLEASE CALL ME

647
00:41:41,670 --> 00:41:42,921
<i>Why aren't you picking up?</i>

648
00:41:43,881 --> 00:41:45,966
<i>Please call me.
Why aren't you answering my call?</i>

649
00:41:46,049 --> 00:41:47,509
<i>Give me a call.
Are you still having dinner?</i>

650
00:41:47,593 --> 00:41:49,511
<i>Honey, when are you coming home?</i>

651
00:41:49,970 --> 00:41:51,054
<i>When are you coming home?</i>

652
00:41:56,185 --> 00:41:57,519
Damn it!

653
00:42:06,278 --> 00:42:07,529
All right, now.

654
00:42:08,197 --> 00:42:10,532
Our best duo, Mr. Son

655
00:42:11,116 --> 00:42:12,826
and Ms. Jeong.

656
00:42:15,871 --> 00:42:17,539
You know that
the launch of the new brand

657
00:42:17,623 --> 00:42:19,583
will decide the fate
of Haemu Foods, don't you?

658
00:42:19,666 --> 00:42:21,084
- Yes.
- I need you two

659
00:42:21,293 --> 00:42:22,878
to work together
and do your best as a team.

660
00:42:22,961 --> 00:42:24,713
- I'll do my best.
- So will I.

661
00:42:24,796 --> 00:42:26,298
- Can you really do it?
- I'll do my best!

662
00:42:26,381 --> 00:42:27,382
Now, cheers!

663
00:42:27,841 --> 00:42:29,259
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

664
00:42:29,343 --> 00:42:30,344
Let's do this!

665
00:42:30,427 --> 00:42:31,720
- Cheers.
- Good luck.

666
00:42:36,391 --> 00:42:37,434
That's nice.

667
00:42:38,060 --> 00:42:39,228
Did you drink yesterday, too?

668
00:42:39,311 --> 00:42:41,146
I really wanted
to keep myself from drinking tonight.

669
00:42:42,105 --> 00:42:43,524
This meat looks nice.

670
00:42:44,399 --> 00:42:46,318
It's beef we're talking about.

671
00:42:51,532 --> 00:42:54,409
<i>Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.</i>

672
00:42:54,493 --> 00:42:56,745
- Damn it.
- <i>You will be charged after the beep.</i>

673
00:42:59,957 --> 00:43:01,083
Darn it.

674
00:43:14,471 --> 00:43:15,806
The work is...

675
00:43:17,641 --> 00:43:18,684
Honey!

676
00:43:23,021 --> 00:43:24,106
I'm sorry.

677
00:43:28,860 --> 00:43:29,903
Darn it.

678
00:43:40,372 --> 00:43:41,373
Jeez.

679
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:45,002
<i>Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected...</i>

680
00:44:30,589 --> 00:44:32,090
What the... Open the door.

681
00:44:32,174 --> 00:44:34,343
Hey! Open the door right now!

682
00:44:34,426 --> 00:44:35,427
I'll kill you.

683
00:44:36,345 --> 00:44:38,472
Open the door! Hey!

684
00:44:38,555 --> 00:44:39,556
Honey.

685
00:44:43,185 --> 00:44:44,311
What are you doing?

686
00:45:12,089 --> 00:45:13,090
Heading home now?

687
00:45:18,011 --> 00:45:19,638
He's so out of it.

688
00:45:20,639 --> 00:45:22,808
He's become a different man
in just a day.

689
00:45:54,089 --> 00:45:55,716
<i>- All right!
- All right!</i>

690
00:45:55,799 --> 00:45:56,842
<i>Great job.</i>

691
00:45:58,176 --> 00:46:00,804
ANXIOUSLY WAITING FOR THE RESULT

692
00:46:00,887 --> 00:46:03,390
CHUNG SANG-HYEON
DROPS FROM 2 STARS TO 1 STAR

693
00:46:05,642 --> 00:46:07,269
<i>The accuracy</i>

694
00:46:07,352 --> 00:46:09,980
<i>of your dance dropped quite a lot
in the verse...</i>

695
00:46:11,523 --> 00:46:14,484
<i>No rank lasts forever in this world.</i>

696
00:46:16,528 --> 00:46:17,571
<i>Hence</i>

697
00:46:19,531 --> 00:46:21,158
<i>the higher your ranking</i>

698
00:46:21,867 --> 00:46:23,160
<i>the more anxious you become.</i>

699
00:46:49,811 --> 00:46:51,271
You're such an embarrassment.

700
00:46:51,521 --> 00:46:53,356
How did you know I was there?

701
00:46:54,065 --> 00:46:55,901
Did you snoop around
every restaurant I might be in?

702
00:46:56,234 --> 00:46:57,527
Why didn't you pick up your phone?

703
00:46:57,611 --> 00:46:59,154
I was having a team dinner!

704
00:47:01,740 --> 00:47:03,742
Can't you pick up your phone
while you eat?

705
00:47:04,201 --> 00:47:05,243
My phone?

706
00:47:06,912 --> 00:47:09,664
Right. You're always
cooped up at home.

707
00:47:09,748 --> 00:47:11,583
You wouldn't understand anything
about work life.

708
00:47:12,250 --> 00:47:14,419
You drive me crazy! Damn it.

709
00:47:22,886 --> 00:47:24,638
<i>If you do not wish to remain weak...</i>

710
00:47:26,765 --> 00:47:28,099
<i>you must fight your way up.</i>

711
00:47:53,583 --> 00:47:55,252
<i>What do you mean...</i>

712
00:47:55,335 --> 00:47:57,045
<i>In the end, keeping your rank</i>

713
00:47:58,713 --> 00:48:00,215
<i>means survival.</i>

714
00:48:02,217 --> 00:48:03,969
<i>Don't lose heart.</i>

715
00:48:06,429 --> 00:48:07,681
<i>Leave no regrets.</i>

716
00:48:08,223 --> 00:48:11,560
What? How did he not make it?

717
00:48:12,811 --> 00:48:15,105
Not only is he
a good singer and a good dancer

718
00:48:15,188 --> 00:48:16,815
but he's good-looking
and is good at everything!

719
00:48:17,315 --> 00:48:20,026
But he's a total ace.
How did he not make it?

720
00:48:20,777 --> 00:48:22,237
How come?

721
00:48:22,320 --> 00:48:23,655
Why?

722
00:49:06,031 --> 00:49:07,032
Excuse me, Mr. Noh.

723
00:49:09,034 --> 00:49:10,702
She has something to report
to the Audit Team.

724
00:49:11,620 --> 00:49:13,371
She's been waiting
since early morning.

725
00:49:19,339 --> 00:49:20,340
It looks like

726
00:49:21,758 --> 00:49:24,135
my husband is having an affair.

727
00:49:24,219 --> 00:49:25,303
Goodness.

728
00:49:26,262 --> 00:49:28,097
When my husband brought home

729
00:49:28,640 --> 00:49:32,519
perfume as a birthday gift,
I knew something was off.

730
00:49:32,602 --> 00:49:34,270
Wait, what about the perfume?

731
00:49:36,689 --> 00:49:39,484
No one buys a perfume
for a married man.

732
00:49:39,567 --> 00:49:40,818
What do you think that means?

733
00:49:41,361 --> 00:49:44,322
It means she wants to mark him
with that scent.

734
00:49:45,406 --> 00:49:48,701
She wants her man
to smell like something she picked.

735
00:49:49,244 --> 00:49:51,538
I've kept my eyes on my husband
since that day

736
00:49:51,621 --> 00:49:53,456
and he never leaves his phone.

737
00:49:53,915 --> 00:49:55,375
He even takes it into the shower.

738
00:49:55,458 --> 00:49:57,752
I read online that it definitely
means he's having an affair.

739
00:50:00,463 --> 00:50:02,173
And they're always working together.

740
00:50:02,674 --> 00:50:04,551
Not only do they
always go on business trips together

741
00:50:04,634 --> 00:50:06,094
but they even message
each other at night.

742
00:50:06,970 --> 00:50:08,721
Right. I have evidence, too.

743
00:50:21,317 --> 00:50:22,860
It's a strand of hair.

744
00:50:25,029 --> 00:50:26,781
I found it on my husband's shirt.

745
00:50:26,864 --> 00:50:29,450
It must belong to that woman.
I know it.

746
00:50:31,995 --> 00:50:33,955
Ma'am, we can't call this evidence...

747
00:50:34,038 --> 00:50:37,375
We'll investigate
and get back to you right away.

748
00:50:38,251 --> 00:50:39,294
Okay.

749
00:50:43,923 --> 00:50:44,924
What?

750
00:50:45,592 --> 00:50:47,844
<i>We must go through the formalities
after receiving a report.</i>

751
00:50:48,094 --> 00:50:51,014
<i>We have to do the paperwork
and talk to the person in question.</i>

752
00:50:51,639 --> 00:50:53,516
<i>What is it? Go and check.</i>

753
00:50:53,891 --> 00:50:54,934
<i>Go, now.</i>

754
00:50:56,769 --> 00:50:58,313
What am I supposed to check?

755
00:50:58,896 --> 00:51:00,857
Should I run a DNA test
on this hair or what?

756
00:51:03,359 --> 00:51:04,527
Come on.

757
00:51:11,576 --> 00:51:12,702
Anyway

758
00:51:13,077 --> 00:51:15,872
wasn't Mr. Son's wife
really frightening last night?

759
00:51:16,331 --> 00:51:18,333
She came all the way there
just because he didn't pick up.

760
00:51:19,042 --> 00:51:21,085
She apparently suspects something
is going on with Ms. Jeong.

761
00:51:21,544 --> 00:51:23,296
Ms. Jeong must feel so wronged.

762
00:51:23,379 --> 00:51:24,505
All she ever does is work.

763
00:51:25,006 --> 00:51:27,675
But I think I understand why.

764
00:51:27,967 --> 00:51:31,012
Couples only see each other
briefly at night.

765
00:51:31,095 --> 00:51:33,598
But you're with work colleagues
all day long

766
00:51:33,681 --> 00:51:35,516
and share more in common.

767
00:51:35,600 --> 00:51:37,602
And you talk to them much more.

768
00:51:38,186 --> 00:51:40,313
I would be concerned, too.

769
00:51:41,105 --> 00:51:42,357
I don't think I'd like that either.

770
00:51:42,565 --> 00:51:44,275
But there are limits.

771
00:51:44,359 --> 00:51:46,194
She was almost delusional.

772
00:51:47,695 --> 00:51:49,489
Gosh. What is this?

773
00:51:50,406 --> 00:51:51,658
She was infamous.

774
00:51:52,325 --> 00:51:54,786
FOOD BRAND PLANNING TEAM

775
00:51:54,869 --> 00:51:57,121
Director Kang will kill us
if we continue like this.

776
00:51:57,205 --> 00:51:59,332
They're exactly
what we agreed to during the meeting.

777
00:51:59,415 --> 00:52:02,460
- Stop making random changes.
- I don't see the point!

778
00:52:03,044 --> 00:52:05,421
Comparing them with domestic brands
isn't what we're doing.

779
00:52:05,713 --> 00:52:08,341
I kept saying that our focus is
on expanding into the global market!

780
00:52:08,424 --> 00:52:09,884
<i>They're just colleagues.</i>

781
00:52:10,385 --> 00:52:11,427
<i>There isn't any affair.</i>

782
00:52:11,678 --> 00:52:13,137
- What?
- Don't you remember?

783
00:52:16,140 --> 00:52:18,559
Let's analyze all corporations
making under a billion won.

784
00:52:19,102 --> 00:52:20,978
- We have to do this.
- Yes, ma'am.

785
00:52:21,104 --> 00:52:24,148
There are some discrepancies
in the business licenses, so...

786
00:52:24,232 --> 00:52:25,608
I see. Really?

787
00:52:29,654 --> 00:52:32,073
Mr. Noh. Come here. Hurry.

788
00:52:38,079 --> 00:52:39,497
- Are we all here?
- Yes.

789
00:52:40,123 --> 00:52:42,417
All right, then. We received

790
00:52:42,792 --> 00:52:45,753
a very important assignment
directly from the top.

791
00:52:45,837 --> 00:52:47,422
- Our team?
- From the top?

792
00:52:47,505 --> 00:52:49,048
Yes, so that means

793
00:52:49,298 --> 00:52:51,718
we must pause whatever we were doing
and handle this first.

794
00:52:52,009 --> 00:52:53,928
This may turn into a criminal case

795
00:52:54,220 --> 00:52:56,973
and blow up into a big story
if anyone outside hears about it.

796
00:52:57,223 --> 00:52:59,100
It must remain confidential

797
00:52:59,684 --> 00:53:02,145
as we resolve the matter
as quietly as possible.

798
00:53:02,228 --> 00:53:03,229
Do you understand?

799
00:53:04,522 --> 00:53:05,606
What is it?

800
00:53:05,982 --> 00:53:08,276
ON-SITE AUDIT TEAM SURVEY
HAEMU GROUP AUDIT TEAM 3

801
00:53:08,568 --> 00:53:09,569
So you're saying

802
00:53:09,986 --> 00:53:11,696
there's poppy here?

803
00:53:11,779 --> 00:53:13,865
Goodness, man.
I told you to be quiet.

804
00:53:15,283 --> 00:53:17,243
The security guard said
he found a poppy out back

805
00:53:17,326 --> 00:53:19,120
while cleaning up the flower bed.

806
00:53:19,203 --> 00:53:20,747
Not the field poppy
but the other kind.

807
00:53:21,164 --> 00:53:23,666
He thinks there may be more
in another place

808
00:53:23,750 --> 00:53:26,461
so we must handle this quietly
before it becomes trouble, okay?

809
00:53:28,421 --> 00:53:29,505
A pharmaceutical company

810
00:53:30,465 --> 00:53:31,507
with a poppy?

811
00:53:32,592 --> 00:53:34,260
Did you eat that flower?

812
00:53:34,761 --> 00:53:36,721
Don't go around eating random stuff
just because it's free.

813
00:53:36,804 --> 00:53:38,556
Goodness. Just keep looking.

814
00:53:47,315 --> 00:53:50,359
- Hello?
- <i>It's Mr. Son's wife calling.</i>

815
00:53:50,443 --> 00:53:52,862
<i>Have you checked the hair?</i>

816
00:53:52,945 --> 00:53:54,864
I'll e-mail you the result.

817
00:53:54,947 --> 00:53:57,033
I'm on a different assignment,
so I must hang up.

818
00:54:10,713 --> 00:54:11,756
Yes?

819
00:54:13,090 --> 00:54:15,551
<i>You said you'd get back to me
after investigating.</i>

820
00:54:16,219 --> 00:54:18,429
<i>I was right, about Ms. Jeong, right?</i>

821
00:54:21,057 --> 00:54:22,850
<i>What will happen to them now?</i>

822
00:54:23,643 --> 00:54:25,561
<i>The company must
handle this strictly to...</i>

823
00:54:25,645 --> 00:54:27,355
Please stop!

824
00:54:29,190 --> 00:54:31,108
Nothing is going on between them.

825
00:54:31,484 --> 00:54:33,861
They're only working hard
even as we speak!

826
00:54:33,945 --> 00:54:35,530
<i>They're together again?</i>

827
00:54:36,656 --> 00:54:38,699
<i>- Did you see them?</i>
- Ma'am.

828
00:54:39,742 --> 00:54:41,619
Please stop pestering me.

829
00:54:42,453 --> 00:54:43,955
You should go see the doctor.

830
00:54:44,038 --> 00:54:46,916
You know, you're being delusional!

831
00:55:01,305 --> 00:55:02,598
You got poop on yourself.

832
00:55:12,024 --> 00:55:13,067
Jeez.

833
00:55:22,618 --> 00:55:24,078
Is the rehearsal
in the conference room?

834
00:55:24,161 --> 00:55:26,080
Yes, I called everyone
and said we were on our way.

835
00:55:26,163 --> 00:55:27,164
- One second.
- Sure.

836
00:55:34,589 --> 00:55:35,631
Thank you.

837
00:55:38,759 --> 00:55:40,261
2. TARGET
SON MYUNG-SOO, JEONG MI-YOUNG

838
00:55:40,346 --> 00:55:41,931
3. METHOD
INTERVIEW, E-MAIL LOGS, CCTV

839
00:56:23,137 --> 00:56:24,555
I hope you bloom and blossom

840
00:56:25,848 --> 00:56:27,350
in this crappy office.

841
00:56:50,331 --> 00:56:52,249
Goodness, Mr. Noh.
Are you getting off now?

842
00:56:57,004 --> 00:56:58,965
I read your report
on Mr. Son Myung-soo's case.

843
00:57:00,049 --> 00:57:01,342
Are you sure that's it?

844
00:57:01,759 --> 00:57:03,552
Are you sure
they aren't having an affair?

845
00:57:04,553 --> 00:57:05,596
No.

846
00:57:06,347 --> 00:57:08,307
How can I be sure
of what's happening between them?

847
00:57:08,724 --> 00:57:10,226
There's no hard evidence

848
00:57:10,559 --> 00:57:12,436
so the circumstantial evidence
points to nothing.

849
00:57:15,523 --> 00:57:17,358
I like how you don't make up crap.

850
00:57:17,817 --> 00:57:21,028
But if this is only between them,
shouldn't you look more into it?

851
00:57:24,323 --> 00:57:25,741
- Hello.
- Hello.

852
00:57:25,825 --> 00:57:28,035
- Food Brand Planning Team?
- Yes.

853
00:57:28,119 --> 00:57:29,328
Are you working overtime?

854
00:57:29,412 --> 00:57:31,706
- Hello.
- Thanks for your hard work.

855
00:57:33,708 --> 00:57:36,502
But I don't see
Mr. Son and Ms. Jeong.

856
00:57:36,585 --> 00:57:38,337
They're getting ready
for the presentation.

857
00:57:38,421 --> 00:57:39,755
We're stepping out to eat dinner.

858
00:57:39,839 --> 00:57:41,298
Is that so?

859
00:57:41,757 --> 00:57:44,010
How do you know everyone in our team?

860
00:57:44,093 --> 00:57:46,220
You're just as they say,
Almighty Joo.

861
00:57:46,637 --> 00:57:49,015
- Almighty Joo?
- It means you have your eyes

862
00:57:49,098 --> 00:57:50,182
on everything and know everything.

863
00:57:50,725 --> 00:57:53,769
Goodness, people say that?
That's crazy.

864
00:57:53,853 --> 00:57:55,187
What? "Almighty Joo"?

865
00:57:56,063 --> 00:57:59,066
But I do know that the Brand Team
is doing something very important.

866
00:57:59,692 --> 00:58:01,861
Okay, since you're all working hard
until late in the night

867
00:58:01,944 --> 00:58:05,489
so I, Almighty Joo, will treat you
to something expensive and delicious!

868
00:58:05,573 --> 00:58:07,033
You are the Almighty Joo!

869
00:58:08,451 --> 00:58:10,911
I'll have it delivered here
for all of you to enjoy

870
00:58:10,995 --> 00:58:12,329
so you can go back upstairs.

871
00:58:12,413 --> 00:58:14,457
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

872
00:58:20,504 --> 00:58:21,547
Good luck.

873
00:58:21,630 --> 00:58:23,049
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

874
00:58:28,345 --> 00:58:30,014
Mr. Noh,
I need a new report from you.

875
00:58:30,222 --> 00:58:31,265
Sorry?

876
00:58:31,348 --> 00:58:34,226
I really must be Almighty Joo.
That's a great nickname.

877
00:58:42,026 --> 00:58:43,611
Why don't we go over our moves again?

878
00:58:45,196 --> 00:58:46,197
Yes, Mr. Son.

879
00:58:51,660 --> 00:58:52,661
But...

880
00:58:58,667 --> 00:58:59,668
what moves do you mean?

881
00:59:06,133 --> 00:59:07,176
Something like this.

882
00:59:28,739 --> 00:59:31,117
What do you mean
you need a new report from me?

883
00:59:31,742 --> 00:59:33,035
You'll find out by tomorrow.

884
00:59:33,536 --> 00:59:35,788
No, maybe today.

885
01:00:09,488 --> 01:00:10,489
Darn it.

886
01:00:23,335 --> 01:00:24,378
Are you all right?

887
01:00:25,588 --> 01:00:26,755
What about you?

888
01:00:28,507 --> 01:00:29,550
What was that?

889
01:00:35,097 --> 01:00:36,182
Darn it.

890
01:00:50,654 --> 01:00:51,906
Mrs. Son...

891
01:01:06,420 --> 01:01:07,463
What did you say?

892
01:01:08,088 --> 01:01:09,131
Delusional?

893
01:01:09,798 --> 01:01:10,925
Damn it.

894
01:01:12,843 --> 01:01:14,845
Why are you only blaming me?

895
01:01:15,721 --> 01:01:18,557
I'm not the one who's crazy.
That asshole and bitch are!

896
01:01:23,354 --> 01:01:24,855
I'm going to kill them.

897
01:02:06,188 --> 01:02:09,108
FILING FOR LOVE

898
01:02:09,692 --> 01:02:12,444
GUEST APPEARANCE
BY PARK HA-SUN, KIM JONG-TAE

899
01:02:37,219 --> 01:02:38,762
{\an8}<i>Mr. Noh is the pride of our team!</i>

900
01:02:39,722 --> 01:02:41,223
{\an8}<i>He says you're the pride.</i>

901
01:02:41,307 --> 01:02:42,474
{\an8}<i>How brazen.</i>

902
01:02:42,558 --> 01:02:44,101
{\an8}If only everyone else were like you

903
01:02:44,184 --> 01:02:46,895
{\an8}this world would've been
a much better place.

904
01:02:48,022 --> 01:02:49,315
{\an8}<i>You're a fool</i>

905
01:02:51,108 --> 01:02:52,693
{\an8}<i>Do your next assignment right.</i>

906
01:02:52,776 --> 01:02:54,945
{\an8}<i>It's Zone F in level four
of the basement parking lot.</i>

907
01:02:56,030 --> 01:02:57,823
{\an8}- We need to expose them.
<i>- Expose?</i>

908
01:02:57,906 --> 01:02:59,658
{\an8}<i>How am I going to do that?</i>

909
01:02:59,742 --> 01:03:02,328
{\an8}Morals? Do you think
you're a police officer or a judge?

910
01:03:02,661 --> 01:03:04,204
{\an8}<i>Do you hate her that much?</i>

911
01:03:04,288 --> 01:03:05,831
{\an8}<i>Should I just quit?</i>

912
01:03:05,914 --> 01:03:08,876
{\an8}<i>You should've talked to me
if you wanted to leave the Audit Team</i>

913
01:03:09,084 --> 01:03:10,461
{\an8}<i>instead of talking behind my back.</i>

914
01:03:25,184 --> 01:03:27,186
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
